@startuml Linkwise_Chat_Relay
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Latin Modern Roman"
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #2A9D8F
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam maxMessageSize 130
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam nodesep 22
skinparam ranksep 28
title UML sequence: asynchronous store-and-forward custody (proposed)
participant "Origin A" as A
participant "Relay R" as R
participant "Destination B" as B
A -> R : message M, final recipient B,\nbounded hop metadata
R -> R : validate relay policy,\ncapacity, expiry and loop\nhistory
R -> R : commit relay copy + custody\nrecord
R --> A : relay_custody receipt (not\nfinal receipt)
... no continuous A-R-B path required ...
R -> R : select later eligible\ncontact; revalidate authority
R -> B : same end-to-end M + updated\nhop metadata
B -> B : validate and commit final\ninbox + receipt
B --> R : final remote-receipt Rb
R -> R : retain Rb for return path;\napply custody retention\npolicy
... later eligible return contact ...
R --> A : forward authenticated Rb
A -> A : validate issuer, message ID\nand digest; mark\nremote_received
note over A,B
Custody is a promise under an explicit
retention/expiry contract.
No deletion on a link ACK; no unlimited receipt or
message forwarding.
Relay failure can leave delivery uncertain; custody
is not a global guarantee.
end note
@enduml
